 {"id": "RELEASE-2026-10-22-02", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "title": "fix(vuln): bump go.mod 'go' directive 1.26.9 -> 1.26.10 — GO-2026-6809/CVE-2026-111943 (eMudhra CA denylist, crypto/x509) is REACHABLE via 'serve' (cmdServe -> http.Server.Serve -> x509.Certificate.Verify); CI red on the release-prep sha; blocks every cut", "reasoning": "RELEASE-2026-10-22-01 (cut v0.1.12, prep sha cd828a23, pushed) is CI-RED on the exact sha to be tagged: CI run 39716231219 FAILURE, job 'Build & Test (1.26)', step Vulnerability-check: 'vulncheck: FAIL — 1 reachable vulnerability found (govulncheck exit 3) GO-2026-6809 (crypto/x509 — fixed in crypto/x509@go1.26.10)'. Independent local confirm on the same tree 2026-10-22: 'make vuln-check' FAIL + raw 'GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 govulncheck -scan symbol ./...' trace '#1: cmd/boardctl/serve.go:130:36: boardctl.cmdServe calls http.Server.Serve, which eventually calls x509.Certificate.Verify' — 'Your code is affected by 1 vulnerability from the Go standard library.' Advisory: GO-2026-6809 = CVE-2026-111943 (compromised eMudhra intermediate CA keys; forged chains verify in unpatched Go); Go 1.26.10 (released 2026-10-19) adds the crypto/x509 denylist. Race proven: 'make vuln-check' on cd828a2 was GREEN (~03:19Z) minutes before the CI run (03:20:24Z) failed — the vuln DB updated between the two runs; the code is unchanged since 1a890b2/9b098e7 (green 39348220207). This is release-blocking: a v0.1.12 cut would ship binaries whose 'serve' verb exposes a reachable x509 verification bypass. Fix (mechanical, same class/pattern as BT-080, commit 3c83aa8 'fix(vuln): bump go 1.26.6 -> 1.26.9'): (1) go.mod:3 'go 1.26.9' -> 'go 1.26.10'; (2) README.md:1216 the Toolchain-requirement sentence (last fixed by README-009/7138683 to 1.26.9) -> 1.26.10 and restate the advisory sentence (GO-2026-6809/CVE-2026-111943, denylist for the compromised eMudhra intermediates) — keep 'do not lower the directive' closing line; (3) 'make vuln-check' green locally, then push: CI green on the new sha. ACCEPTANCE: go.mod line 3 = 'go 1.26.10'; grep README.md '1.26.10' present + no stale 'go 1.26.9' toolchain sentence; make vuln-check (and full gate battery fmt-check/version-check/spec-check) exit 0; gh run on the push = success for BOTH workflows; RELEASE-2026-10-22-01 then becomes unblockable (same cut, v0.1.12, extended range includes the fix commit).", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["go", "security", "ci", "release"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-22T03:22:06.33221+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T05:47:18.703653+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a6726fd6b6135498bbabc23ac57767b55689265c857699f30691a86afb109d07", "evidence": [{"run_id":"39716231219","ts":"2026-10-22T03:22:06.33221+00:00"},{"run_id":"0f4b634b","ts":"2026-10-23T05:47:18.703653+00:00"}]}, "foreman_note": null, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "fbcc6a4", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "go.mod bumped 1.26.9 -> 1.26.10; README toolchain sentence updated; govulncheck clean; go build/vet/test -short all green; TestVulncheck passes without GOTOOLCHAIN override; pushed fbcc6a4 to origin/main; gitreins Tier-2 PASS verdict 0f4b634b", "depends_on": ["RELEASE-2026-10-22-01"], "acceptance": "make vuln-check in /home/kara/coding-hermes-boardctl exits 0 (the target compiles internal/vulncheck/vulncheck_test.go TestVulncheck; exit non-zero or a reachable govulncheck finding means the row is not done); awk 'NR==3' go.mod prints exactly 'go 1.26.10'; grep -n 'go 1.26.10' README.md returns a match on the toolchain-requirement sentence (near line 1369, 'The toolchain requirement: go.mod declares') and no line there still says 'go 1.26.9'"}
